Third-party software and assets used by free-renew
===================================================

This project (free-renew, https://github.com/yangshu114514/free-renew)
builds upon the following third-party works. Each is used under the terms
of its own license; this file summarizes attributions required by those
licenses and by fair-practice conventions.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. BookerLiu/FreeServer (author: Demo-Liu / GitHub user BookerLiu)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Source:    https://github.com/BookerLiu/FreeServer
  License:   Apache License 2.0
  Use:       Protocol knowledge. The "cmd=" form protocol spoken by
             api.sanfengyun.com and api.abeiyun.com (login.php / renew.php,
             the check_free_delay / free_delay_list / free_delay_add command
             family, the ptype and yanqi_img field names) was originally
             documented by FreeServer in 2020 and re-verified against the
             live services in 2026.

  Statement: This project is an independent reimplementation in Rust.
             No source code from FreeServer is included or copied.
             Per Apache-2.0 Section 4, this file serves as the
             attribution notice for that project's protocol documentation.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. rust-headless-chrome (headless_chrome crate)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Source:    https://github.com/rust-headless-chrome/rust-headless-chrome
  License:   MIT
  Use:       Direct dependency (Chrome DevTools Protocol client). Used for
             the article-page screenshot and its bundled stealth-mode
             bypasses (webdriver/chrome-runtime/plugins/permissions/webgl),
             which this project enables via tab.enable_stealth_mode().
  Note:     Attribution per MIT Section 2 (copyright + permission notice
             retention is satisfied by this file and LICENSE).

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. gautamkrishnar/keepalive-workflow (GitHub Action)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Source:    https://github.com/marketplace/actions/keepalive-workflow
  License:   MIT
  Use:       GitHub Actions workflow step (.github/workflows/renew.yml).
             Prevents GitHub's 60-day auto-disable of scheduled workflows
             by appending a no-op commit when the repository is inactive.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. CSDN x-ca signing constants (public frontend constants)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Source:    CSDN web editor bundle; documented in the community at
             https://cloud.tencent.com/developer/article/2420128
  Use:       x-ca-key (203803574) and the appSecret
             (9znpamsyl2c7cdrr9sas0le9vbc3r6ba) are public constants
             embedded in CSDN's own web frontend. Referenced as protocol
             constants, not creative work.

